<title>USA: Soros asks antitrust okay for more WMX shrs.</title>
<headline>Soros asks antitrust okay for more WMX shrs.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by U.S. investor George Soros said Thursday it sought antitrust clearance to acquire additional shares in WMX Technologies.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it filed the request under the Hart-Scott-Rodino Antitrust Improvements Act with the Federal Trade Commission and the Department of Justice on March 13.</p>
<p>The group holds about a 5.2 percent stake in the Oak Brook, Ill., garbage hauling company.</p>
